{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"ALSA-2026:95367","published":"2026-11-04T00:00:00Z","modified":"2026-11-05T20:15:03.816587333Z","related":["CVE-2026-64378","CVE-2026-72080","CVE-2026-72221","CVE-2026-72222","CVE-2026-74586","CVE-2026-89488","CVE-2026-90315","CVE-2026-98974"],"upstream":["CVE-2026-64378","CVE-2026-72080","CVE-2026-72221","CVE-2026-72222","CVE-2026-74586","CVE-2026-89488","CVE-2026-90315","CVE-2026-98974"],"summary":"Important: kernel security update","details":"The kernel packages contain the Linux kernel, the core of any Linux operating system.  \n\nSecurity Fix(es):  \n\n  * kernel: writeback: fix race between cgroup_writeback_umount() and inode_switch_wbs() (CVE-2026-64378)\n  * kernel: sunrpc: pin svc_xprt across the asynchronous TLS handshake callback (CVE-2026-72222)\n  * kernel: sunrpc: wait for in-flight TLS handshake callback when cancel loses race (CVE-2026-72221)\n  * kernel: fs/resctrl: Fix use-after-free during unmount (CVE-2026-72080)\n  * kernel: sctp: clear new_transport when removing a peer (CVE-2026-74586)\n  * kernel: openvswitch: Fix CT limit teardown use-after-free (CVE-2026-89488)\n  * kernel: PCI/sysfs: Add lockdown checks to legacy I/O and memory handlers (CVE-2026-90315)\n  * kernel: kernel: xfs: Unauthorized data modification via improper file size exchange handling (CVE-2026-98974)\n\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n","affected":[{"package":{"name":"kernel","ecosystem":"AlmaLinux:10","purl":"pkg:rpm/almalinux/kernel"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"6.12.0-211.74.1.el10_2"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/AlmaLinux/osv-database/blob/master/advisories/almalinux10/ALSA-2026:95367.json"}},{"package":{"name":"kernel-64k","ecosystem":"AlmaLinux:10","purl":"pkg:rpm/almalinux/kernel-64k"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM